meta {
  name: Post isochrone
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/isochrone
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "lat": 41.3874,
    "lon": 2.1686,
    "mode": "pedestrian"
  }
}

docs {
  Returns walk/drive-time isochrone polygons around a point, via Valhalla.

  Body:
  - `lat` float, required, -90..90
  - `lon` float, required, -180..180
  - `mode` string, required, one of `pedestrian` | `auto`

  Point must fall within the Catalonia bounding box (`min_lat: 40.5, max_lat: 42.9, min_lon: 0.15, max_lon: 3.4`)
  or the request 400s.

  Contours computed: 5 / 10 / 15 minutes (see `CONTOUR_MINUTES` in `api/app/config.py`).

  Response: GeoJSON `FeatureCollection`. Each Feature is one contour polygon with
  `properties.contour` (minutes) and `properties.color`.

  Cached in Redis for 1h, keyed by rounded lat/lon/mode — repeat calls with the
  same input return instantly from cache.

  Errors:
  - 400 coordinate outside Catalonia bbox
  - 502 Valhalla error
}
